        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Anna Ranch Heritage Center; Waimea; Hawaii County; Hawaii; United States\n- People: Anna Leialoha Lindsey Perry-Fiske\n- Topics: cattle ranches; census-designated places; population\n\nFacts:\n- Anna Leialoha Lindsey Perry-Fiske was born in 1900 and died in 1995.\n- Anna Ranch Heritage Center is a former cattle ranch in Waimea, Hawaii County, Hawaii, and it was named for Anna Leialoha Lindsey Perry-Fiske.\n- Waimea is a census-designated place in Hawaii County, Hawaii, United States.\n- Waimea had a population of 7,028 at the 2000 census.\n- Waimea had a population of 9,212 at the 2010 census.",
